# Keep CRLF for the VBS forwarder on checkout — a repository convention, not a
# requirement. WSH treats CR, LF and CRLF alike as line terminators: an LF-only
# forwarder runs correctly under both cscript and wscript (measured 2026-11-14).
# The encoding that does break it is a UTF-8 BOM (800A0408); see CONTEXT.md.
# `text eol=crlf` normalises to LF in the index and restores CRLF on checkout.
*.vbs text eol=crlf

# PowerShell reads either ending fine, but keep the authored bytes as-is.
*.ps1 -text
